1.      kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
kubectl
Reads deployment.yaml
API Server (Authentication + Authorization + Validation)
Stores Deployment in etcd
Deployment Controller notices new Deployment
Creates ReplicaSet
ReplicaSet creates Pods
Scheduler assigns Pods to Worker Nodes
Kubelet receives Pod specification
Container Runtime pulls image
Container starts 
Pod becomes Running

2.kubectl apply -f service.yaml
kubectl
Reads service.yaml
API Server
Validation
Stores Service in etcd
Service Controller detects Service
Creates ClusterIP
kube-proxy updates iptables/IPVS rules
Service starts routing traffic
Traffic reaches matching Pods

3.   kubectl get deployments or kubectl get pods
kubectl
HTTPS Request
API Server
Reads information from etcd
Returns current status
kubectl prints output
